    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d219">

                <pb facs="0380" n="284" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg284"/>

                <head>No. 219.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hale
                        to Mr. Bassett.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 26,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 106.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Your dispatch No. 131, of the 10th instant,
                    relative to the Jastram affair, has been received. The Department congratulates
                    you that <pb facs="0381" n="285" xml:id="pg285"/> the energy and perseverance
                    with which you have followed up that difficult case has at last been crowned
                    with success, and that it has been adjusted upon a basis compatible with the
                    honor of both Governments.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES HALE,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
